{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{lyricist: Thomas O. Chisholm}
{composer: William M. Runyan}
{year: 1923}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune FAITHFULNESS}
{meta: meter 11.10.11.10 with refrain}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to FAITHFULNESS}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags faithfulness, morning}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Great is Thy [Bm]faithful[Em]ness, [A7]O God my [D]Father;
[D]There is no [B7]shadow of [Em]turning with [A]Thee;
[A7]Thou changest [D]not, Thy com[D7]passions, they [G]fail not;
[G]As Thou hast [D]been, Thou for[A7]ever wilt [D]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Great is Thy [G]faithful[D]ness!
[Bm]Great is Thy [E7]faithful[A]ness!
[D]Morning by [G]morning new [D]mercies I [A]see;
[A7]All I have [D]needed Thy [D7]hand hath pro[G]vided;
[G]Great is Thy [D]faithfulness, [A7]Lord, unto [D]me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Summer and [Bm]winter and [Em]springtime and [A7]harvest,
[D]Sun, moon and [B7]stars in their [Em]courses a[A]bove
[A7]Join with all [D]nature in [D7]manifold [G]witness
[G]To Thy great [D]faithfulness, [A7]mercy and [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Pardon for [Bm]sin and a [Em]peace that en[A7]dureth,
[D]Thine own dear [B7]presence to [Em]cheer and to [A]guide;
[A7]Strength for to[D]day and bright [D7]hope for to[G]morrow,
[G]Blessings all [D]mine, with ten [A7]thousand be[D]side!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
